### A.2 DeebLorenz

The DeebLorenz database consists of three systems and four observation schemes and is separated into tuning and testing data with 10 and 100 replications, respectively.

Each system is described by an autonomous, first-order, three-dimensional ODE of the form

| | | | | --- | --- | --- | | | u˙​(t)=f⁡(u⁡(t)),for ​t∈ℝ,\dot{u}(t)=f(u(t))\,,\quad\text{for }t\in\mathbb{R}\,, | |

u˙​(t)=f⁡(u⁡(t)),for ​t∈ℝ,\dot{u}(t)=f(u(t))\,,\quad\text{for }t\in\mathbb{R}\,,

where f:ℝ3→ℝ3f\colon\mathbb{R}^{3}\to\mathbb{R}^{3} is the vector field ff and the solution u:ℝ→ℝ3u\colon\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}^{3} describes the state of the system over time. For the three systems, the vector field ff are created as follows:

